{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You shall not learn to do.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: but you may learn to understand and to instruct. And so we find concerning the seventy of the Sanhedrin, that they were required to be expert in all wisdoms, even in the wisdom of sorcery, so that they might judge every matter with true judgment according to the law of the Torah; and had they not been complete in the wisdom of knowing every kind of sorcery, and even one kind were lacking that they did not know, they would not have been able to render judgment for liability or for exemption and to apply the law to it accordingly."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:09.001656425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}